<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.6.1: Interpreting Statements in Function Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00941</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.6.1: Interpreting Statements in Function Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3964ba4f-76a0-4d37-99d3-9b335e002531</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Diego is walking home from school at a constant rate. This graph represents function \(d\), which gives his distance from home, in kilometers, \(m\) minutes since leaving the school.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Use the graph to find or estimate:</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
        <figure id="fig-00001">
          <media alt="Graph of line. Horizontal axis, 0 to 24 by 4’s, minutes since leaving school. Vertical axis, 0 to 3 by point 5’s, kilometers from home. Line starts at about 0 comma 2 point 2 5, and ends at 20 comma 0.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">What is \(d(0)\), and what does it represent in the situation?
</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005"/>
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00007">\(d(0)=2.25\); Zero minutes after Diego has left school, he is 2.25 kilometers from home, or Diego’s school is a little more than 2 kilometers from his house.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">\(d(12) =\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00009"/>
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00011">\(d(12)=0.9\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012">What does \(d(m)=1\) mean in the context of the problem, and what is \(m\)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00013"/>
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00015">\(m\) is approximately 10.5. After approximately 10.5 minutes, Diego is 1 kilometer from home.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00016">What does \(d(m)=0\) mean in the context of the problem, and what is \(m\)?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00017"/>
          <para id="para-00018">Compare your answers:</para>
          <para id="para-00019">\(m\) is 20. After 20 minutes, Diego is 0 kilometers from home, or it takes Diego 20 minutes to walk the 2.25 kilometers home from school.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>